FINDINGS: #C1405 at f9b5f65d. S1 (medium, Worker CPU): OWNER_WAIT in worker/board-rules.mjs is quadratic on whitespace: '\s+(?:for\s+)?(?:a|an|the)?\s*(?:decision|pick)' lets \s+ and \s* split one run of spaces every way. A paused write whose next_note is 'wait' + 100k spaces takes 7.7 s in waitsOnOwner; next_note has no length cap in cardWriteRefusal and the body cap is ~20 MB, so one store write can hold the Worker past its CPU limit. Fix: '(?:(?:a|an|the)\s+)?(?:decision|pick)' (1M chars in 2 ms, same answers on the card's cases), and/or cap next_note before the test; add a timing test. Rest is fine: the owner's name is built, not written; ctx.asks is open asks only; no route or page change. Security 2026-11-20.
